  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Npc133119 may interact with Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through multiple indirect pathways. The first path links Npc133119 to Natural resistance-associated macrophage protein 2, which is targeted by a complex compound, and this compound further targets Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. The second path connects Npc133119 to ADP-ribosylation factor-like protein 3, which is targeted by (-)-Fragransin A2, which also targets Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. The third path similarly links Npc133119 to Natural resistance-associated macrophage protein 2, which is targeted by another compound that also targets Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. These findings suggest that Npc133119 may act as a modulator or activator of pathways that ultimately lead to the inhibition of Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. The evidence supports a mechanism where Npc133119 influences the activity of downstream targets that are directly or indirectly involved in the regulation of Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase.",
